{
  "title": "JLR SDD 169 authoritative diagnostic data (306DT/AJD-V6D diesel PCM + platform)",
  "provenance": {
    "package": "SDD_169.00.001_FULL.exe (InstallShield/MSI; payload data2.cab, group CURRENT_JLR_XCL_XML_DATA_XML)",
    "encryption": "Per-file 3DES-ECB. Key = first 24 bytes of nibble-swapped blob embedded in Environment.dll CCryptFile ctor (RVA 0x1000) = ASCII 'YmZwZlQrQ3V4dVltNTArWE9s'. PKCS5 padding. CryptImportKey PLAINTEXTKEYBLOB alg CALG_3DES(0x6603), KP_MODE=ECB(2).",
    "source_files": {
      "module_address_map": "Xml/L494_201600/<MODULE>.exml (decrypted) -> moduletype + CAN srcId/targetId",
      "pcm_dids": "Xml/L494_201600/MDX_PCM_D_3LT.exml and MDX_PCM_D.exml (decrypted)",
      "scr_routines": "Xml/L494_201600/MDX_SCR.exml (decrypted; ECU_NAME=PCM)"
    },
    "validated_against": "Live capture VIN SALWA2EK8HA162826 (2017 L494 3.0 SDV6), captures/jlr/car-sweep-*.json 2026-08-18"
  },
  "notes": [
    "SDD names only a curated subset of DIDs (37 for the diesel PCM); the ECU physically answers ~191. Absence from this list does NOT mean a DID is dead.",
    "0x7E6 is the ABS module on L494 (request 0x7E6 / response 0x7EE), NOT an SCR/reagent controller. No separate SCR ECU exists in the L494 CAN map; SCR/reagent is managed by the PCM at 0x7E0.",
    "042C (DPF soot, g/l, inferred from differential pressure) IS a defined diesel-PCM DID in SDD, but the L494 SALWA2EK8HA PCM did not answer it (dead on this calibration). Read frame is 22 04 2C.",
    "Urea/SCR DIDs 05FA-05FD live-answered on the PCM: this is the reagent-system telemetry for the AdBlue job."
  ],
